==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|los}}, from {{inh|en|ang|los||damage, destruction, loss}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*los}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*lusą||dissolution, break-up, loss}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lews-||to cut, sunder, separate, loose, lose}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|is|los||dissolution, looseness, break-up}}, {{cog|ang|lor}}, {{m|ang|forlor||loss, ruin}}, {{cog|gmh|verlor||loss, ruin}}. More at {{l|en|lose}}.

