====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} The result of no longer possessing an object, a function, or a characteristic due to [[external]] causes or [[misplacement]].
#: {{syn|en|expense}}
#: {{ant|en|gain}}
#: {{ux|en|'''loss''' of limb; weight '''loss'''; '''loss''' of cognitive functions; '''loss''' of appetite.}}
#: {{ux|en|People are less willing to [[take a risk]] to make a gain than to avoid a '''loss'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2018-10-28|title=China's Melting Glacier Brings Visitors, Adds to Climate Concerns|work=[[w:Voice of America|VOA Learning English]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260519000323/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/china-s-melting-glacier-brings-visitors-concern-over-climate-change/4627742.html|text=In other areas, glacier '''loss''' creates serious risk of a dry period across the Third Pole, Wang said.}}
#*: [[File:In other areas, glacier loss creates serious risk of a dry period across the Third Pole, Wang said.ogg]]
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[destruction]] or [[ruin]] of an object.
# {{lb|en|countable}} Something that has been destroyed or ruined.
#: {{ux|en|It was a terrible crash; both cars were total '''losses'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|defeat}}{{lb|en|countable}} [[defeat|Defeat]]; an instance of being [[defeat]]ed.
#: {{ant|en|win|victory}}
#: {{ux|en|The match ended in their first '''loss''' of the season.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[death]] of a person or animal.
#: {{ux|en|We mourn his '''loss'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The battle was won, but '''losses''' were great.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[condition]] of [[grief]] caused by losing someone or something, especially someone who has [[die|died]].
#: {{ux|en|Her daughter's sense of '''loss''' eventually led to depression.}}
# {{lb|en|financial|countable}} The [[sum]] an entity loses on balance.
#: {{ant|en|profit}}
#: {{ux|en|The sum of expenditures and taxes minus total income is a '''loss''', when this difference is positive.}}
# {{lb|en|engineering}} Electricity of kinetic [[power]] expended without doing useful work.
#: {{ux|en|The inefficiency of many old-fashioned power plants exceeds 60% '''loss''' before the subsequent '''losses''' during transport over the grid.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When ''loss'' is used in a genitive/possessive construction to denote that a thing (X) is lost, this is often constructed as ''loss of (X)'' rather than ''(X)'s loss''.
* ''loss'' is often the object of the verbs {{m|en|make}} or {{m|en|take}}. See [[Appendix:Collocations of do, have, make, and take]]

